"[0711.0330] Assessing statistical significance of periodogram peaks (https://arxiv.org/abs/0711.0330)\nciteturn210view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/0711.0330\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 168\nL0: 【0†Search】 【1†Submit】 【2†Donate†info.arxiv.org】 【3†Log in】\nL1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · 【4†Advanced search】\nL5: \nL6: # Astrophysics\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 2 Nov 2007]\nL9: # Title:Assessing statistical significance of periodogram peaks\nL10: \nL11: Authors:【5†Roman V. Baluev】\nL12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Assessing statistical significance of periodogram peaks, by Roman V. Baluev\nL14: \nL15: 【6†View PDF】 【7†HTML (experimental)】\nL16: > Abstract: The least-squares (or Lomb-Scargle) periodogram is a powerful tool which is used routinely in many branches of astronomy to search for periodicities in observational data. The problem of assessing statistical significance of candidate periodicities for different periodograms is considered. Based on results in extreme value theory, improved analytic estimations of false alarm probabilities are given.\nL17: They include an upper limit to the false alarm probability (or a lower limit to the significance). These estimations are tested numerically in order to establish regions of their practical applicability.\nL18: Comments:  | 7 pages, 6 figures, 1 table; To be published in MNRAS\nL19: Subjects:  | Astrophysics (astro-ph)\nL20: Cite as:  | 【8†arXiv:0711.0330】 [astro-ph]\nL21:    | (or 【9†arXiv:0711.0330v1】 [astro-ph] for this version)\nL22:    | 【10†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.0711.0330†doi.org】 arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: Journal reference:  | Mon. Not. R. Astron. Soc., 2008, Vol. 385, Issue 3, pp. 1279-1285\nL24: Related DOI (Digital Object Identifier):  | 【11†https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-2966.2008.12689.x†doi.org